code protocol_electrum::get_scripthash_history(address_subscription& sub,
    const hash_digest& hash, size_t limit) NOEXCEPT
{
    BC_ASSERT(notification_strand_.running_in_this_thread());

    histories history{};
    const auto& query = archive();
    if (const auto ec = query.get_history(stopping_, sub.cursor, history,
        hash, limit, turbo_))
        return ec;

    if (history.empty())
        return error::success;

    auto it = history.cbegin();
    while (it != history.cend() && it->confirmed())
        write_status(sub.accumulator, *it++);

    midstate copy = sub.accumulator;
    while (it != history.cend())
        write_status(copy, *it++);

    sub.status = copy.flush();
    return error::success;
}

text:
After all that, the fully optimized implementation is fundamentally just this method. This is running on the channel's notification strand. `stopping_` is an atomic bool that gets set via socket (or process) termination on the main channel strand, passed into the expensive query for cancellation. `sub.cursor` is now a height-based cursor, and r/w parameter to the query, which updates each read to the top of the chain, so most reads will only accumulate one block of confirmed related txs. The `limit` parameter is from config, and will terminate the query with an error if the number of address outputs exceeds that value (though it can really handle any volume). `turbo_` is also config, allowing the store query to be run on all available threads (across the set of potentially millions of outputs). The hash accumulator `sub.accumulator` is stored with the cursor and the last status hash `sub.status` on the subscription (`144 bytes` + `32 byte scripthash key` for each subscription of the channel). The accumulator is copied after the confirmed txs are appended to it, and the unconfirmed are then accumulated and flushed as the next `sub.status`, which is then sent  as the notification if it has changed.
```code protocol_electrum::get_scripthash_history(address_subscription&amp; sub,
    const hash_digest&amp; hash, size_t limit) NOEXCEPT
{
    BC_ASSERT(notification_strand_.running_in_this_thread());

    histories history{};
    const auto&amp; query = archive();
    if (const auto ec = query.get_history(stopping_, sub.cursor, history,
        hash, limit, turbo_))
        return ec;

    if (history.empty())
        return error::success;

    auto it = history.cbegin();
    while (it != history.cend() &amp;&amp; it-&gt;confirmed())
        write_status(sub.accumulator, *it++);

    midstate copy = sub.accumulator;
    while (it != history.cend())
        write_status(copy, *it++);

    sub.status = copy.flush();
    return error::success;
}```
